{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1494147","title":"16S rRNA V1V3 Amplicon Sequencing of the Korean Scalp Microbiome in Cicatricial Alopecia","description":"This BioProject contains 16S rRNA gene amplicon sequencing data generated from scalp microbiome samples collected from Korean patients with neutrophilic primary cicatricial alopecia, including dissecting cellulitis (DC) and folliculitis decalvans (FD). Samples were collected using three sampling methods (swab, hair pluck, and scalp biopsy) to compare bacterial community composition across specimen types. The V1V3 region of the bacterial 16S rRNA gene was sequenced on the Illumina MiSeq platform using paired-end sequencing. Air swab samples were included as negative controls to monitor potential environmental contamination during sample collection and processing.","center":"Jeonbuk National University Hospital","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2026/07/13 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN61595832","Air-exposed Copan swab negative control collected during sampling of subject CA60 (060NCXUSw220221)","probable_urban","air_dust","2022-02-21",2022,"KR","Jeollabuk-do",1845457,"Jeonju","verified",35.8469,127.1413,"South Korea: Jeonju","environmental air","sampling environment","sampling environment","sterile sampling device","city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN61595833","Air-exposed Copan swab negative control collected during sampling of subject CA61 (061NCXUSw220221)","probable_urban","air_dust","2022-02-21",2022,"KR","Jeollabuk-do",1845457,"Jeonju","verified",35.8469,127.1413,"South Korea: Jeonju","environmental air","sampling environment","sampling environment","sterile sampling device","city-level location without sample-site c